s & Logic Gates**#Video 3":[17,23],"#**Unit 1 – Number Systems & Logic Gates**#Video 3#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/JQBRzsPhw2w\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[19,23],"#**Unit 1 – Number Systems & Logic Gates**#Video 3#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/JQBRzsPhw2w\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: Introduces Boolean algebra and logic simplification, explains XOR/XNOR gates, and demonstrates their use in circuits.":[20,23],"#**Unit 1 – Number Systems & Logic Gates**#Video 3#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/JQBRzsPhw2w\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: Introduces Boolean algebra and logic simplification, explains XOR/XNOR gates, and demonstrates their use in circuits.#{1}":[22,23],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**":[24,37],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 1":[25,27],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 1#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ol8D69VKX2k\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[26,27],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 1#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ol8D69VKX2k\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: Functional units of a computer: ALU, Control Unit, Memory, Input/Output devices, and their interactions in instruction execution.":[27,27],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 2":[28,30],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/bM2PyN-EIS0\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[29,30],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/bM2PyN-EIS0\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: Detailed explanation of addressing modes, memory access, and instruction sequencing in assembly language":[30,30],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 3":[31,37],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 3#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZW1gb3h-f9k\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[33,37],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 3#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZW1gb3h-f9k\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: RISC vs CISC architectures: differences, advantages, instruction sets, and performance comparisons.":[34,37],"#**Unit 2 – Basic Structure of Computers**#Video 3#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZW1gb3h-f9k\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: RISC vs CISC architectures: differences, advantages, instruction sets, and performance comparisons.#{1}":[36,37],"#**Unit 3 – ALU Design**":[38,45],"#**Unit 3 – ALU Design**#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/RuKkePyo9zk\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[41,45],"#**Unit 3 – ALU Design**#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/RuKkePyo9zk\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: IEEE-754 floating-point format: representation, normalization, rounding, and basic arithmetic operations in ALUs.":[42,45],"#**Unit 3 – ALU Design**#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/RuKkePyo9zk\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: IEEE-754 floating-point format: representation, normalization, rounding, and basic arithmetic operations in ALUs.#{1}":[44,45],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**":[46,56],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**#Video 1":[48,50],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**#Video 1#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/1mlohB3WL18\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[49,50],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**#Video 1#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/1mlohB3WL18\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: Pipelining in CPUs, performance improvement, types of hazards (data, control, structural) and strategies to resolve them.":[50,50],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**#Video 2":[51,56],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/CDO28Esqmcg\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[52,56],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/CDO28Esqmcg\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: Control unit design: hardwired vs microprogrammed, generation of control signals, instruction execution cycles.":[53,56],"#**Unit 4 – Control Unit & Pipelining**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/CDO28Esqmcg\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: Control unit design: hardwired vs microprogrammed, generation of control signals, instruction execution cycles.#{1}":[55,56],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**":[57,66],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**#Video 1":[58,60],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**#Video 1#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/0eJU9EzyNUo\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[59,60],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**#Video 1#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/0eJU9EzyNUo\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: ARM Thumb instruction set: compressed instruction format, memory load/store instructions, and simple I/O operations.":[60,60],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**#Video 2":[61,66],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7LqPJGnBPMM\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>":[62,66],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7LqPJGnBPMM\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: ARM architecture fundamentals: ARM5 and ARM7 core architecture, CPU cores, instruction encoding, and pipeline overview.":[63,66],"#**Unit 5 – Parallelism & ARM**#Video 2#<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7LqPJGnBPMM\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe>#Description: ARM architecture fundamentals: ARM5 and ARM7 core architecture, CPU cores, instruction encoding, and pipeline overview.#{1}":[65,66]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"updated_at":"2025-11-17T19:53:16.161+05:30","edited_seconds":630},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"9qdjyv","at":1781247494318},"key":"Sem 3/COA/COA YT Videos.md"},
